  "worked_solution": "Since $f(x)$ is left-continuous at $x=-1,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=f(-1)=-6.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}(2f(x)-xf(-1)) & =2{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)-f(-1){lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}x \\\\  & =2(-6)-(-6)(-1) \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
